<p>The statue was originally installed along Main Street in the center of the east depot park. It moved to its current location, centered on Main Street at Third Avenue, during construction of the <a href="/places/landmarks/northern-pacific-colonial-depot/">Colonial depot</a> in 1930. The wooden flagpole from Fort Abraham Lincoln was also moved to the depot ellipse. It eventually deteriorated and was replaced by the present metal flagpole.</p>

