<p>Roosevelt briefly served as a Morton County deputy sheriff. Sheriff {% person "george-harmon" %}George Harmon{% endperson %} authorized him to pursue three men accused of stealing his 16-foot boat from the Elkhorn Ranch during a wintry April 1886. Roosevelt subdued them without a fight and brought them to Mandan for trial. One was released, and two received five-year prison sentences in the Bismarck penitentiary. Because of the cold, Roosevelt did not bind their hands or feet. He borrowed a wagon and walked guard behind them for 36 hours without sleep before stopping in Dickinson.</p>
